  "identifier": "hf-ehr",
  "name": "hf_ehr",
  "description": "HuggingFace-native framework for training large language models on structured electronic health records using the MEDS (Medical Event Data Standard) format. Ships pretrained autoregressive foundation models — GPT, Llama, Mamba, and Hyena architectures — trained from scratch on 2 billion tokens of de-identified structured EHR data from Stanford Health Care. Designed for researchers already in the HuggingFace ecosystem who want to fine-tune or benchmark EHR foundation models without custom pipelines. Complementary to FEMR: FEMR covers masked/CLMBR-style training; hf_ehr covers autoregressive HuggingFace-native training. FEMR's own documentation recommends hf_ehr for autoregressive CLMBR-style models. Apache 2.0. From the Shah Lab at Stanford Medicine.",
  "url": "https://github.com/som-shahlab/hf_ehr",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/som-shahlab/hf_ehr",
